WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.875
I think some of
the damage I did

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:11.644
is probably permanent as far
as like an enlarged heart.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:12.712
Yeah.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.280
I don't want to go
back and bodybuild.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.582
I'm not looking for that.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:18.118
I'm looking for how
long can I live, right?

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.887
I mean if you look around
this office, who's here?

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:22.021
It's old man.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.556
It's like why am I here?

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:24.391
I'm freaking 37.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.126
I mean something's wrong, right?

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.895
Jeff has been under the
care of a cardiologist

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.397
for the past year.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:34.033
Ever since doctors treating
his steroid infection also

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.636
discovered signs
of heart failure.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.705
So, Doctor, because
Jeff took testosterone

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:39.572
for so many years--

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.707
Right.

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.475
Now his body doesn't
produce it naturally.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:43.910
And he actually has to take
testosterone to stay healthy.

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:45.445
Right.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.814
This is the unfortunate irony
for guys that are looking

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:50.316
to become superhuman per say.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.051
They end up in a
point where, again,

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.254
they obliterate their
body's own ability

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.822
to produce testosterone.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:59.959
Today, Jeff will be getting
the results to see if his heart

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.294
has bounced back to normal.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.363
So there's two
main things that we

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.497
are evaluating with that echo.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.766
One is your systolic
function which

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.268
is the squeezing function.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.637
And that was the one that
was mildly reduced last time

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:11.871
you were here.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.707
That actually does not look
significantly different.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:15.975
OK.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:16.876
So it still looks a
little bit sluggish.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.111
Yep.

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.246
But there's another
parameter that we

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.715
look at which is the relaxation
function of the heart.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.050
Right.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:25.485
And that was also quite
abnormal last time you

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:26.319
got here.

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:27.587
That looks significantly better.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:28.421
OK.

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:29.823
OK.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.891
You know we're not at the point
where I'd say your heart looks

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:32.792
normal, unfortunately.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.360
Right.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:35.929
I think you should sort of
get your mind around the fact

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:40.767
that you're probably going to
be on long term medication.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.735
I worry about Jeff's longevity.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:46.105
His heart actually hasn't
bounced back to normal.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:49.509
And the longer we see it, that
sort of suggests that something

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:50.777
permanent has happened there.

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:53.279
And if he started
taking steroids again?

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.882
Not a good idea.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:57.917
We heard from a lot of
people that say that there

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.319
is a safe way of doing this.

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:00.820
The people that have
gotten hurt is because they

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.088
didn't know what
they were doing,

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.057
and they were taking
too much, or--

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:05.692
but there is actually
a safe way to do this.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:06.326
Right.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.660
What do you think?

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.562
I think those people
are kidding themselves.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:13.032
The best data that we
have are autopsy studies.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:15.034
That means someone died.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:17.170
Jeff, frankly, is lucky.

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.172
There's lots and
lots of case reports

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:21.107
of young guys
having heart attacks

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:24.177
and having strokes,
sudden death.

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:26.746
So your first symptom is dying.

